Notes on the sketch of a normative ethic

    moral law, conditions
        : note: these according to one or another of the various divine-command theories of morality,
          divorced of its supernatural assumptions, with the creator in place of God
        a) a command (addressed demand) of our creator
        b) the creator’s backing of it by force
    moral law, conditions that hold
        a) a command (addressed demand) of our creator
            : join @ `^^moral law, conditions$`
            - reason addresses to us a demand (to endure)
            - this demand is proper also to our creator
                ∵ our creator backs it by force
                    : join `^*- the creator forces.+us.+to conform`
                / what more evidence [of the demand] could we expect?
            - the addressing of the demand is proper also to our creator
                ∵ our creator advertises to us a reminder of the demand
                    ∵ bright stars on every clear night advertise it
                    ∵ this is by design of the creator
                / what more evidence [of the addressing] could we expect?
            ∴ this condition holds
        b) the creator’s backing of it by force
            : join @ `^^moral law, conditions$`
            - the creator forces on us a predisposition|tendency to conform (to endure)
                ∵ in creating us, the creator uses natural selection
                ∵ natural selection ingrains within us a tendency to endure
                ∵ natural selection makes real the power of a) an awareness of having been cared for
                  by our creators *as their brood* to forcefully remedy b) our present failure
                  to care for ourselves *as a species*
                    : re `(a\).+awareness.+\*as their brood\*).+(remedy b\).+failure.+\*as a species\*)`s
                      cf. `^*- ${1} might ${2}$`p @ `^*. what speaks for an action plan` @
                      ~/work/ethics/applied/._/text.notes.brec
                    ∵ natural selection makes real the power of d) a group’s experience of being loved
                      or cared for *as a group* to inform and enforce e) the practice of loving or caring
                      for themselves as a group
                        : re `(the power of d\).+\*as a group\*).+(e\) the practice.+as a group)`s
                          cf. `^*∵ of ${1} to enable ${2}$`p @ `^*. what speaks for an action plan` @
                          ~/work/ethics/applied/._/text.notes.brec
                    - this fits our concept of promulgated law
                        : see @ `^*∴ effecting awareness \(a\) suffices to animate.+the whole works` @
                          ~/work/ethics/applied/._/text.notes.brec
                        ∵ there the promulgation of a command as a writ suffices to enforce it
                          — through a pre-existing apparatus of power — as law
                        ∵ here an awareness of the creator’s care for us suffices to impel our self care,
                          again through a pre-existing apparatus of power
                            - the creator’s will [for us] in the form of the imperative of the safehold
                              is a command, a ‘writ’ in the sky, that we are forced to obey
                            ∴ it is law
            ∴ this condition holds
